193
00:20:30,201 --> 00:20:44,160
So then he says, the Buddha says, it is in this way that the bhikkhu is an arahat with tanks destroyed, one who's lived the holy life, done what had to be done and been liberated through final knowledge.

194
00:20:46,974 --> 00:20:51,601
When a bhikkhu's mind is thus liberated, he possesses three unsurpassable qualities.

195
00:20:51,701 --> 00:20:54,684
Unsurpassable vision, that's meant to be nirvana.

196
00:20:54,825 --> 00:20:56,567
Unsurpassable practice of the way.

197
00:20:56,907 --> 00:21:01,933
So in other words, he knows how he got there and the path to liberation.

198
00:21:01,953 --> 00:21:06,720
And unsurpassable deliverance, that he won't return back to the ordinary life.

199
00:21:07,500 --> 00:21:13,548
When a bhikkhu is thus honoured, he still honours and reveres and venerates the Tathagata.

200
00:21:13,568 --> 00:21:16,813
So he still venerates me as the blessed one.

201
00:21:17,096 --> 00:21:20,901
The Blessed One is enlightened and teaches the Dharma for the sake of enlightenment.

202
00:21:21,061 --> 00:21:25,185
The Blessed One is tamed and teaches the Dharma for taming oneself.

203
00:21:25,606 --> 00:21:29,570
The Blessed One is at peace and teaches the Dharma for the sake of peace.

204
00:21:29,590 --> 00:21:33,296
The Blessed One has crossed over and he teaches the Dharma for crossing over.

205
00:21:33,715 --> 00:21:36,479
This is crossing over to the island.

206
00:21:36,680 --> 00:21:42,125
And the Blessed One has attained Nibbana and he teaches Dharma for the attaining of Nibbana.

207
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:50,701
Now, when this was said, Sachika replied, Master Gautama, we were bold and impudent in thinking we could attack Master Gautama in debate.

208
00:21:51,541 --> 00:22:00,113
A man might attack a mad elephant and find safety, yet he could not attack Master Gautama and find safety.

209
00:22:00,834 --> 00:22:08,383
A man might attack a blazing mass of fire and find safety, yet he could not attack Master Gautama and find safety.

210
00:22:08,818 --> 00:22:16,750
A man might attack a terrible poisonous snake and find safety, yet he could not attack Master Gautama and find safety.

211
00:22:17,151 --> 00:22:21,958
We were bold and impudent in thinking we could attack Master Gautama in debate.

212
00:22:22,740 --> 00:22:24,102
So final capitulation.

213
00:22:24,501 --> 00:22:29,730
So he says, let the Blessed One come with the Sangha of Bhikkhus and consent to a meal tomorrow.

214
00:22:31,297 --> 00:22:51,313
and so he then turns to the chavis this is uh the neganthus son sachika and says you know bring along food for the for the feast you see and then there's a lovely bit at the end in the morning of course the blessed one dresses takes his bowl and makes his way to where the meal is in the uh at the head of a group of monks

215
00:22:51,782 --> 00:23:04,157
And Satyaka Niganta's son took a low seat, sat by the side, said to the Blessed One, Master Gautama, may the merit and the great meritorious fruits of this act of giving be for the happiness of the givers.

216
00:23:04,917 --> 00:23:06,480
So that's mainly the Licchavis.

217
00:23:07,101 --> 00:23:18,253
And Ajivisena, the Buddha replies, whatever comes about from giving to a recipient such as yourself, one who is not free from lust, not free from hatred, not free from delusion.

218
00:23:18,795 --> 00:23:20,777
So remember, he was thought of as a saint.

219
00:23:21,247 --> 00:23:45,751
that will be for the givers and whatever comes about from giving to a recipient such as myself one who is free from lust free from hate free from delusion that will be for you so he's he's saying that uh he there's a special merit that will accrue to satchika because he's offered food to somebody who is completely liberated

220
00:23:46,103 --> 00:23:47,686
So a nice little ending there.

221
00:23:48,808 --> 00:23:50,373
Poor old Sachik has been humbled.

222
00:23:50,894 --> 00:23:52,617
He was, what was it now?

223
00:23:52,679 --> 00:24:00,096
He was sitting very glum and dejected and he's finally lifted up out of it, recognized his mistake.

224
00:24:01,695 --> 00:24:05,119
and come to some pleasant ending with the Buddha.

225
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:08,523
So you have to take this as a pinch of salt.

226
00:24:08,683 --> 00:24:10,326
It's a little bit of Buddhist propaganda.

227
00:24:11,066 --> 00:24:19,055
The Buddha had these two sort of big groups that he would generally have to debate against.

228
00:24:19,194 --> 00:24:25,122
First of all, the Brahmins and their position as

229
00:24:25,320 --> 00:24:52,019
special priests and stuff like that and their beliefs and on the other side was the uh with the james you see so uh i can only hope this uh discourse has been at least some light relief uh we have been over some of the old um teachings there about not self uh and i can only hope that uh you will carry on your practice and become fully liberated sooner rather than later

230
00:24:53,603 --> 00:24:55,444
so we can begin our practice.

231
00:25:09,181 --> 00:25:20,673
Pudanku Jaini Dhamanku Jaini

232
00:25:26,340 --> 00:25:51,436
SANGAM PUJAYI NAMO TASA VAGWATO ARAHATO SAMMA SAMBUDASA NAMO TASA VAGWATO ARAHATO SAMMA SAMBUDASA

233
00:25:52,278 --> 00:26:21,474
Namo Tassa Bhagavato Agahato Sambha Sambhudasa Bodhansaranangacchami Dhammansaranangacchami Sanghansaranangacchami Dutiyampi Bodhansaranangacchami

234
00:26:22,078 --> 00:26:47,529
Tuthiyampi Dhamam Saranam Gacchami Tuthiyampi Sangam Saranam Gacchami Tuthiyampi Bodham Saranam Gacchami Tuthiyampi Dhamam Saranam Gacchami

235
00:26:48,201 --> 00:27:13,128
Kati Ampi Sanggang Saranam Gacchami Panati Pata Veramani Sikapada Samadhi Ami Adina Dana Veramani Sikapada Samadhi Ami

236
00:27:13,597 --> 00:27:22,290
Kame sumi cacera, veramani sikapadam, samadhi ami.

237
00:27:23,132 --> 00:27:30,962
Musa wada, veramani sikapadam, samadhi ami.

238
00:27:31,784 --> 00:27:41,157
Sura meraya, maja pamadhatana, veramani sikapadam.

239
00:27:41,137 --> 00:28:02,318
So we're making sure that our posture is that of the fully liberated one.

240
00:28:08,265 --> 00:28:11,127
Now just that moment to lift the energy

241
00:28:12,121 --> 00:28:18,128
Up from the lower back and abdomen, lifting up, up through the top of the head.

242
00:28:20,353 --> 00:28:22,434
Gently, no strain.

243
00:28:22,476 --> 00:28:26,461
And relaxing the brow.

244
00:28:26,500 --> 00:28:29,685
Eyes gently closed.

245
00:28:33,049 --> 00:28:34,913
Lips together, teeth apart.

246
00:28:38,397 --> 00:28:39,259
Shoulders.

247
00:28:43,255 --> 00:28:44,376
And hands on the lap.

248
00:28:49,945 --> 00:28:55,955
Just acknowledging that posture, the energy running up the spine, everything else.

249
00:28:57,759 --> 00:29:04,230
Relax.

250
00:29:04,250 --> 00:29:07,255
This body is subject to disease.

251
00:29:10,880 --> 00:29:39,519
This body is of a nature to fall ill This body has not gone beyond sickness This body is subject to aging This body is now in the process of aging

252
00:29:45,962 --> 00:29:49,346
This body has not gone beyond aging.

253
00:29:56,875 --> 00:29:58,636
This body is subject to death.

254
00:30:04,463 --> 00:30:06,885
This body has not gone beyond death.

255
00:30:13,193 --> 00:30:15,395
This body will die.

256
00:30:21,046 --> 00:30:27,895
There is the unborn, undying, uncreated, uncompounded.

257
00:30:33,684 --> 00:30:34,766
The unconditioned.

258
00:30:37,931 --> 00:30:40,295
True refuge, harbour and home.

259
00:30:43,779 --> 00:30:45,923
Perfect peace and contentment.

260
00:30:52,535 --> 00:30:56,279
Those who are mindful are in the presence of Nirvana.

261
00:31:04,150 --> 00:31:11,799
Waiting for the settlement and then opening up to whatever draws the attention within that field of awareness.

262
00:31:13,502 --> 00:31:19,150
Just observing, just feeling, just experiencing.

263
00:31:21,744 --> 00:31:25,787
Keeping awake that sense of curiosity.

264
00:31:28,702 --> 00:31:29,426
That's enough.

265
01:05:38,099 --> 01:06:05,355
A moment's reflection Resolution

266
01:06:22,750 --> 01:06:26,173
So we can begin our evening contemplations.

267
01:06:33,061 --> 01:06:37,766
So just speaking gently into our own hearts.

268
01:06:42,871 --> 01:06:45,534
May I be free from physical pain.

269
01:06:49,565 --> 01:06:53,177
May I be free from mental distress.

270
01:06:58,695 --> 01:07:01,887
May I be liberated of all my sufferings.

271
01:07:38,840 --> 01:07:42,246
Bringing to mind someone we know who's going through a hard time.

272
01:07:48,836 --> 01:07:51,400
May you be free of physical pain.

273
01:07:58,393 --> 01:08:00,797
May you be free of mental distress.

274
01:08:08,101 --> 01:08:10,516
May you be liberated of all your suffering.

275
01:08:53,899 --> 01:08:58,225
And for all those at this moment who are sick and or suffering from mental illness.

276
01:08:59,908 --> 01:09:06,197
People in the process of dying and those who have died and left grieving family, relatives and friends.

277
01:09:08,000 --> 01:09:11,024
People going hungry, homeless and destitute.

278
01:09:13,346 --> 01:09:17,672
Those having to deal with severe personal and interpersonal difficulties.

279
01:09:19,735 --> 01:09:23,180
All those caught up in wars and repressive regimes.

280
01:09:24,072 --> 01:09:50,603
and those being tortured and there are those suffering from natural disasters and climate crisis all the sentient beings are being cruelly treated and unnecessarily slaughtered and all who find life painless may you be free of physical pain

281
01:09:56,792 --> 01:09:59,122
May you be free of mental distress.

282
01:10:04,341 --> 01:10:06,869
May you be liberated of all your sufferings.

283
01:10:40,110 --> 01:10:43,795
offering our compassion to all beings in all directions.

284
01:10:44,536 --> 01:10:47,519
May all beings be free of physical pain.

285
01:10:53,305 --> 01:10:55,967
May all beings be free of mental distress.

286
01:11:02,494 --> 01:11:05,899
May all beings be liberated of all their sufferings.

287
01:11:37,317 --> 01:11:42,962
Bring to mind now some moments of joy, happiness that we've experienced today.

288
01:11:55,435 --> 01:11:56,555
And rejoicing in that.

289
01:11:58,377 --> 01:11:59,720
May I be joyful.

290
01:12:04,064 --> 01:12:06,126
May my joyfulness increase.

291
01:12:11,488 --> 01:12:14,867
May I experience the bliss of liberation.

292
01:12:48,967 --> 01:12:51,911
Bring to mind someone we know is caused to be joyful.

293
01:12:51,970 --> 01:13:01,280
May you be joyful.

294
01:13:04,783 --> 01:13:06,747
May your joyfulness increase.

295
01:13:12,192 --> 01:13:14,875
May you experience the bliss of awakening.

296
01:13:42,917 --> 01:14:05,904
And all those at this moment who are happy and content with their lives, who enjoy the warmth of friendships, delight in art and nature, hobbies and so on, who find their work meaningful, who enjoy the fruitfulness of their spiritual lives and who rejoice in the success of others.

297
01:14:08,407 --> 01:14:09,667
May you be joyful.

298
01:14:14,018 --> 01:14:15,886
May your joyfulness increase.

299
01:14:21,509 --> 01:14:24,180
May you experience the bliss of Nirvana.

300
01:14:51,261 --> 01:14:56,791
Radiating our goodwill joy to all beings in all directions.

301
01:14:56,930 --> 01:14:59,815
May all beings be joyful.

302
01:15:05,645 --> 01:15:07,507
May your joyfulness increase.

303
01:15:13,979 --> 01:15:17,404
May you experience the bliss of Nirvana.

304
01:15:42,157 --> 01:15:44,498
I need words now to flow through us.

305
01:15:46,740 --> 01:15:59,854
If you are wise and want to reach the state of peace, you need to be upright, responsible, gentle and humble, easily contented and need only a few things.

306
01:16:00,814 --> 01:16:04,438
Not always be busy and have the right sort of work.

307
01:16:05,559 --> 01:16:08,502
You need to guard the senses and be modest.

308
01:16:10,827 --> 01:16:14,953
You do not have to be exclusively attached to only a few people.

309
01:16:16,255 --> 01:16:20,280
You should not do the slightest thing that a wise person could blame you for.

310
01:16:21,502 --> 01:16:22,685
Be always thinking.

311
01:16:22,784 --> 01:16:33,000
May all beings be happy, whatever living beings there are, be they weak or strong, big or small, large or slender, living nearby or far away.

312
01:16:33,921 --> 01:16:37,006
Those who've already been born and those who've yet to be born.

313
01:16:37,046 --> 01:16:39,670
May all beings, without exception,

314
01:16:40,104 --> 01:16:40,786
Be happy.

315
01:16:41,926 --> 01:16:46,390
Be truthful to one another and do not think anyone anywhere is of no value.

316
01:16:47,231 --> 01:16:55,600
Do not wish harm to anyone, even when you're angry, just as a mother would protect her only child at the risk of her own life.

317
01:16:55,619 --> 01:17:01,006
So you should let the warmth of your heart go out to all beings.

318
01:17:01,025 --> 01:17:07,631
Let your thoughts of love go through the whole world, above and below, without any barrier, with no ill will or hatred.

319
01:17:08,523 --> 01:17:16,755
whether you're standing, walking, sitting, or lying down, so long as you are awake, develop this affectionate mindfulness.

320
01:17:18,377 --> 01:17:20,479
This, they say, is the noblest way to live.

321
01:17:20,640 --> 01:17:37,724
And if you do not fall into unskillful ways, but live well and develop insight, and are no longer attached to all the desires of the senses, then truly, you'll never need to be reborn into this world again.

322
01:17:37,743 --> 01:17:38,444
So,

323
01:17:38,914 --> 01:17:46,386
Please join me in the chant or if you wish, continue offering your goodwill using perhaps these traditional blessings.

324
01:17:47,067 --> 01:17:49,350
May you be safe, well and happy.

325
01:17:49,930 --> 01:17:53,735
May you live contented in harmony with the world.

326
01:17:56,199 --> 01:18:08,618
Karaniyagatakusalena Yantang Santang Padang Gavisamecha Sakujucha Suhujucha

327
01:18:08,952 --> 01:18:38,064
Suvacchocca samudu anattimani Santu sakoca subharoca Apacchocca salahukkavuti Santendroca nipakoca Apagabokkalesu ananuhido Nacchakutansamacchalekenshi E na venyu pare upavate

328
01:18:38,820 --> 01:19:01,807
Sukhino vākemi noham tu Sābe satāpavāntu sukhi tātā Nāparo parāṅgni kubhē tā Nāti mānyatā kathā cilēṅ kañcī Vīyārosāṅ na pātigāsāṅ yā Nānyā mānyā sādukāṅ gīcchē yā

329
01:19:02,614 --> 01:19:29,516
matāyātāniyāṁ pūṭhaṁ gāyūsāikā pūṭhaṁ gānurāke he vāṁpi sāvabhūteṣu manāsāṁ bhāvāye āparīmanāṁ me tencā sāvālokāsmiṁ manāsāṁ bhāvāye āparīmanāṁ udhāṁ adho cārthirīyaṁ ca

330
01:19:29,969 --> 01:19:33,833
Asampatanga verangasapatam.

331
01:19:34,635 --> 01:19:43,167
Tithancharanasinovasayanavayavatasavigatamido.

332
01:19:43,186 --> 01:19:50,355
Heitansatingaditeyaprakmangetangviharangitamahu.

333
01:19:51,377 --> 01:19:58,186
Ditinchaanupagamasilavadasanenasampano.

334
01:19:58,824 --> 01:20:11,434
May all beings be happy.

335
01:20:12,088 --> 01:20:40,425
I think I missed a bit of the chanting there, sorry about that.

336
01:20:40,927 --> 01:21:01,265
must be tired so uh don't forget from now to fall asleep is also part of our practice and putting something quite lovely into the heart slipping away into sweet oblivion only to wake up in the morning to take full advantage of the day may you sleep peacefully

